# Hellfrost (warlock)
Sci-fi automation hardcore game. C++20 headless engine + React/TypeScript web client, JSON-RPC 2.0 over WebSocket.

Full documentation: CLAUDE.md

## Stack
- Engine: C++20, EnTT (ECS), Sol2+Lua5.4, IXWebSocket, cereal, nlohmann/json, magic_enum
- Web: React 19, TypeScript, Vite, Zustand, Pixi.js, Dockview, Monaco Editor
- Build: CMake + just. `just run` / `just test-e2e` / `just web-dev`

## Architecture
Web UI → JSON-RPC (:9800) → C++ Handler → EnTT registry → 50ms systems → broadcast → Zustand → React

## Critical Rules
- Ask questions before implementing. Never rush to code.
- Search before creating — duplicates are the main failure mode.
- Run `just test-e2e` after any C++ change.
- Never modify `data/` or `save/` directories.
- No code comments unless truly non-obvious.
- Report features done only after end-to-end verification.

## Serialization Footgun
field_save() and field_load() MUST have identical fields in identical order. COMPONENT_LIST macro is the single source of truth for serialization.

## Key Files
- include/game/components/frame.hpp — core structs
- include/game/component_registry.hpp — COMPONENT_LIST macro
- src/rpc/handlers/ — RPC method implementations
- scripts/components/ — Lua component definitions
- web/src/stores/game.ts — game state
- web/src/rpc/types.ts — TypeScript DTOs
